{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1174031-serious-mind-control","id":1174031,"title":"Serious mind control","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-07T08:26:14-08:00","id":1174031,"title":"Serious mind control","content":"I am not sure, whether this doesn't fall into the &quot;ask a question, get an answer&quot; category.<br /> <br /> What arcana are needed to perform such tasks as:<br /> <br /> - Completely reprogramme someone's memories, to the point that the person in question have tens or even hundreds of years rewritten.<br /> - Place someone in an illusion so overwhelming that it amounts to being trapped in the Martix. I.e., completely replace sensory input with illusions, rather than simply add new elements to the sensory input.<br /> <br /> Would you allow such effects with Mind 5 or is it only within the scope of archmastery? The description of &quot;Mind Wipe&quot; essentially implies that the first shouldn't be really possible to execute for regular masters. Would you allow it with some extra means? (Other than casting Mind Wipe a couple hundred times on the same subject).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-07-2018, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T08:40:01-08:00","id":1174035,"title":"","content":"I would say these both falling into the category of Archmastery.<br /> <br /> Additionally, they're also acts of Hubris (obviously). Given the severity, I would reduce Wisdom by 1 without allowing a roll at all each time they're used, but if you're not comfortable with things the rules don't have precedent for rolling 1 die would be acceptable I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T08:52:49-08:00","id":1174038,"title":"","content":"Check out Read the Depths, it would require multiple castings of Indefinite Duration for the effects to stick, but it does modify memory. I'd allow a spell based on Psychic Reprogramming (Or just add a +1 Reach option to that spell) that can affect a number of memories equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> Another route that doesn\u2019t require as much magic is to connect via Telepathy to your target and then do an Astral dive to their Oneiros and see what you can do from there.<br /> <br /> As for the illusion, Hallucination has you covered. Make sure to add the senses beyond the base five like proprioception, kinesthesia, etc. If the subject is a Mage they\u2019ll probably figure it out eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T09:55:22-08:00","id":1174053,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't let you do it via a spell, but I'd allow going on an extended &quot;Mindscaping&quot; project through their Oneiros to accomplish it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:03:45-08:00","id":1174058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1174031-serious-mind-control?p=1174053#post1174053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't let you do it via a spell, but I'd allow going on an extended &quot;Mindscaping&quot; project through their Oneiros to accomplish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not disagreeing with you, just taking a variation, I'd allow the spell, but I'd make the mindscaping in the Oneiros more reliable and harder to undo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T13:17:47-08:00","id":1174119,"title":"","content":"My reasoning was that since Mind 5 already allows for memory editing affecting a couple of months, then some variations of that spell (possibly via effects of combined Arcana? maybe Mind 5 + some Time?) should allow to broaden this scope.<br /> <br /> As for the illusion effect, I believe that Mind 6 should be enough (a spell that would dynamically create new illusions depending on the actions of the subject seems right in the scope of the Practice of Dynamism). I thought that this might be available even at Mind 5 via Practice of Making. <br /> <br /> I am somewhat surprise about the claims that such large-scope mind manipulation shouldn't be possible via spells at all. Could you elaborate on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T14:06:17-08:00","id":1174129,"title":"","content":"There's a servant-faction the Seers have that do the first one.<br /> <br /> The Ministry of Paternoster has access to an Abyssal entity called the Tutor that can basically take a human and erases their soul. It's still there but damaged, and everything about the person is gone. They have consciousness gems that allow them to then imprint certain personalities with sets of skills and attributes and even histories onto them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T15:25:09-08:00","id":1174137,"title":"","content":"The Tutor is from Lower Depths but aside from that everything checks out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}